  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscComm 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "At your local cancer center\u2019s research open house, a research team
    shares early ideas for new cancer treatments. You speak up about the importance
    of affordable treatment options that support patients\u2019 quality of life.
    \r\n\r\n<b>In this situation, what role does a community advocate play in early
    research?</b>"
  explanation: "By sharing the patient perspective early on, community advocates
    help researchers focus on what matters most to patients and the community. This
    guidance can shape research priorities before preclinical studies begin. By speaking
    up about patients\u2019 needs and experiences, advocates help ensure early research
    addresses real-world concerns and has meaningful impact for the people it aims
    to help."
  correctAnswer: Sharing patient priorities to help guide how research ideas are
    shaped
  incorrectAnswer1: Voting on which drug compounds the research team should test
    next
  incorrectAnswer2: "Approving the research team\u2019s study so it can move forward"
  incorrectAnswer3: "Helping manage the team\u2019s lab experiments and data collection"
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
